  "query_preview": "..\n\nLongwave ridging in place over much of the southern two thirds of \nNorth America will persist through the upcoming weekend and into the \nbeginning of next week. The weather narratives are: continuing dry \nweather, daytime highs some 5 to 10 degrees above normal, and near \nnormal low temperatures. Plenty of sunshine is expected. The flow \npattern is projected to be quite weak over the next 5 days which \nbrings the potential for fog and br during each of the nighttime and \ndaybreak periods. Overall likelihood of fog during any particular \nmorning will be dependent on flow direction and whether a location \nwill be directly downstream of the Great Lakes. Introduced patchy \nfog in the forecast for the morning period Thursday through Monday.\n\nThe only minor blip to the ridging will be a weak surface trough \nextending southward from the Hudson Bay. Forecast data supports the \nthe weak trough or saddlepoint pushing through the area between 06-\n12z tonight. The change to the sensible weather will be a prevailing \neasterly wind direction that will set up post weak front Thursday.",
